// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// BANKED RED (unregistered — the effects audit's tail_join face,
// 2026-07-31). The SIBLING of mn-scc-false-negation with NO recursion
// anywhere: `both` calls two effect-polymorphic callees, so their two
// instantiated row vars meet in one frame and tail_join (effects.mn:418-425)
// keeps the FIRST, dropping the second with no constraint recorded.
// `quiet_first` declares `!TZ` and transitively performs TZ through its
// SECOND argument — passes, and the medium teaches "tighten further".
//
// The discriminator is ORDER, not position: `both_rl` accumulates the
// same two callees in the opposite order and refuses correctly, with the
// noisy callee in the identical parameter slot. Measured on boot
// 3c0ee1a1 (e2042bdd).
//
// LEG-CONTRACT NOTE for graduation: the control (`noisy_first`) already
// refuses, so a naive class-reports read is GREEN today — the leg must
// assert BOTH declarations refuse (two E_EffectMismatch lines; today's
// RED is exactly one, plus the false tighten-invitation on the silent
// twin). Greening condition: tail_join records the union of two var
// tails as an EDGE (mint v3, bind both into it) instead of returning
// the first — the rung-3 landing stated over accumulation.
//
// Distinct from mn-scc-false-negation: no binding group is involved, so
// a fix that makes a GROUP's charges draw edges leaves this reachable.
// Greens when tail_join records the union of two tails as an edge — mint
// v3, bind both into it — instead of returning the first.
effect TZ {
  tz() -> Int
}

fn apply1(f) = f()

fn apply2(g) = g()

fn both_lr(f, g) = apply1(f) + apply2(g)

fn both_rl(f, g) = apply2(g) + apply1(f)

fn quiet_one() = 1

fn noisy() = tz()

fn quiet_first() with !TZ = both_lr(quiet_one, noisy)

fn noisy_first() with !TZ = both_rl(quiet_one, noisy)

fn main() = 0
